/storage/
# What the upload tests write. They run with the api module as their working directory, and
# the rule above anchors to the repository root, so it misses this. The whole directory rather
# than a line per kind of picture: the list was one behind every time a kind was added or
# renamed, and the only thing that is ever written here is a test's own scratch. The event
# banners committed under it long before this rule stay tracked, as an ignore never un-tracks.
services/api/storage/
private
**/.yarn
.playwright
.playwright-mcp
backups
.kotlin
*.md
# release-please maintains the changelog, and a contributor editing it would
# otherwise have the change silently dropped by `git add`.
!CHANGELOG.md
!docs/changelogs/*.md
# docs/ is tracked prose — ADRs and flow docs. Without this, adding a new one is
# silently dropped by `git add` and only noticed when the file is missing from
# the PR. Proposals stay ignored: they are working documents, not repo record.
!docs/**/*.md
docs/proposals/**
# The shipped art's credit files. The attribution is published wherever the images
# are, so the row for each file travels with it — both beside the shipped masters and
# beside the working folder the masters are cut from.
!gameart/CREDITS.md
!services/api/src/main/resources/db/seed/esports/art/CREDITS.md
!services/api/src/main/resources/db/seed/boards/art/CREDITS.md
.idea
*dump.sql*

# env files (*.env and .*.env anywhere under services/ or tests/)
services/**/.*.env
services/**/*.env
tests/**/.*.env
tests/**/*.env

# image build secrets and generated output
/vps/.env
/vps/cloud-init/cloud-config.yaml
/vps/cloud-init/cloud-config-standalone.yaml
/vps/cloud-init/rendered/
/vps/.test-cache/
/vps/packer/output/
/backup/

# infra secrets
/infra/.infra.env

# platform/ is the GitOps tree and must always be fully tracked;
# negate the broad patterns above that would otherwise eat it.
!platform/
!platform/**
# GHCR pull-PAT used during v2 bring-up
.ghcr_token
.cf_token
